    <innerclass refid="classterminal_1_1_i_term2_decoder" prot="public">terminal::ITerm2Decoder</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceterminal">terminal</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>iTerm2 OSC 1337 inline image decoder. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classterminal_1_1_i_term2_decoder" kindref="compound">terminal::ITerm2Decoder</ref></computeroutput> parses an OSC 1337 <computeroutput><ref refid="classFile" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/doxygen/doc/juce.tag">File</ref>=</computeroutput> payload and produces an <computeroutput>ImageSequence</computeroutput> with all frames in RGBA8 format. JUCE handles base64 decoding; the platform-native codec (<computeroutput>loadImageSequenceNative</computeroutput>) handles image decoding including animated GIF frame extraction. A JUCE-based fallback path handles formats not supported natively.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Protocol summary</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">ESC<sp/>]<sp/>1337<sp/>;<sp/><ref refid="classFile" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/doxygen/doc/juce.tag">File</ref>=[key=value;...]<sp/>:<sp/>&lt;base64&gt;<sp/>BEL</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> Key=value pairs (separated by <computeroutput>;</computeroutput>, terminated by <computeroutput>:</computeroutput>):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="group__juce__audio__plugin__client-Unity_1ga010e50efcb9d6d393b9414f09f368dbc" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/doxygen/doc/juce.tag">name</ref>=&lt;base64&gt;</computeroutput> — filename (ignored)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>size=&lt;bytes&gt;</computeroutput> — declared file size (ignored)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>width=&lt;spec&gt;</computeroutput> — display width (ignored — Step 11 polish)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>height=&lt;spec&gt;</computeroutput> — display height (ignored — Step 11 polish)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>preserveAspectRatio=N</computeroutput> — 0 or 1 (ignored — Step 11 polish)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>inline=N</computeroutput> — 0 = skip (download only), 1 = display inline</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="structterminal_1_1_image_sequence" kindref="compound">terminal::ImageSequence</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classterminal_1_1_sixel_decoder" kindref="compound">terminal::SixelDecoder</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>terminal::Parser::onImageDecoded </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
